From a4e358721f858a776fd35268462e416bdac1a760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 05:00:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add dnshealth module: wildcard DNS health validation for exit
 relays

New scanning module that detects broken DNS resolution on Tor exit relays
using a wildcard DNS technique.

Unlike the existing dnsresolution module (which queries fixed domains and
cannot distinguish caching from relay-specific failures), dnshealth
generates unique-per-relay DNS queries ({uuid}.{fp_prefix}.{base_domain})
against a configurable wildcard DNS record.  This eliminates caching
effects and provides definitive per-relay DNS health status.

Features:
- Wildcard mode (default): query unique subdomain, verify expected IP
- NXDOMAIN mode (fallback via -H flag): query random UUID subdomain,
  treat NXDOMAIN as success (DNS is working)
- Configurable retry logic with per-attempt timeouts
- Hard timeout protection via SIGALRM
- Structured JSON output per relay for automated analysis
- Circuit failure and terminated relay tracking in teardown()
- All settings configurable via environment variables

The wildcard domain defaults to tor.exit.validator.1aeo.com but MUST be
configured for deployment via DNS_WILDCARD_DOMAIN and DNS_EXPECTED_IP
environment variables.

Usage:
    exitmap dnshealth                    # wildcard mode
    exitmap dnshealth -H example.com     # NXDOMAIN fallback mode

Includes 60 unit tests covering query generation, result structure,
SOCKS error parsing, mode detection, retry logic, hard timeouts,
environment variable configuration, and teardown behavior.

Also updates doc/HACKING.md to document the first_hop parameter and
teardown() kwargs available to all modules.

Co-authored-by: 1aeo <1aeo@users.noreply.github.com>
